r-esp32-evil: port hooks for the ESP32-S3 / QEMU / host-simulator targets

Every change is behind a macro that the upstream Windows and Linux builds do
not define, so with none of them set the decomp builds exactly as upstream:

  RE1_PORT_TASKSWITCH_EXTERNAL  TaskScheduler.cpp takes its three switch
                                primitives from the port (FreeRTOS tasks on
                                Xtensa, where ucontext does not exist)
  RE1_PORT_OVERRIDE_RAND        rand()/srand() override as on Linux (newlib)
  RE1_PORT_VIDEO_RV1            movies may be re-encoded ".rv1" files
  RE1_SMALL_MEM                 fit 8 MB of PSRAM (and the scarce internal
                                RAM: the never-written room sound table goes
                                to flash): large function-local
                                scratch statics become call-scoped heap
                                buffers (PortMem.h), port-only headroom is
                                trimmed, the PAK LZW dictionary is packed and
                                lives only while a background unpacks
  RE1_BG_ON_DEMAND              read each camera's background at the cut
                                instead of caching every camera (768 KB)
  RE1_TMD_MAX_TRIS_COLLECT      size of the per-frame TMD triangle pool
  RE1_PORT_TEXTURE_BGR555       display_image hands 15-bit pixels to the
                                backend (no 300 KB RGBA copy per camera cut)
  RE1_PORT_TEXT_SCALE           the font upload tells the backend which
                                texture is the game font (text layer)
  RE1_PORT_TEXTURE_INDEXED      mask / effect pages go to the backend as PS1
                                indexed pixels (no 256 KB RGBA copy per cut)
  RE1_PORT_VRAM16               the item/menu VRAM pages are kept at 16 bits
  RE1_PORT_EXTRAS               OPTIONS > EXTRAS (text size, give item,
                                invincible, invisible, FPS counter)
  RE1_PORT_TEXTURE_PAL8         model skins and effect pages are flagged as
                                palette art (8-bit storage in the backend)
  RE1_PORT_BENCH                OPTIONS > BENCHMARK: a room tour through
                                every room and camera (no cutscenes, no
                                NPCs), with load times and frame rates on
                                the console; re1bench_goto / re1bench_camera
                                jump to a room and camera by command
  RE1_PORT_PROFILE              per-frame time buckets for the [PERF] line
                                and work counters for the [WORK] line
                                (PortProf.h -> port/include/re1_prof.h)
  RE1_PORT_FAST                 same output, less work: the sprite queue is
                                not re-sorted (nor re-checked) when already in
                                order and a depth range is found by binary
                                search; the model pipeline reuses its scratch,
                                drops primitives wholly off the screen before
                                lighting them, lights only the vertices of
                                drawn triangles, divides without a library
                                call (re1_fastmath.h), writes compact sort
                                keys as it emits and draws the sorted pool in
                                place (MarniDX::DrawTriangles3DList); on the
                                ESP32 its hot loop runs from IRAM (RE1_HOT_FN)

